---
// Generated from the product OPERATOR manual's own symptom table.
// Styled to the composite's troubleshooting archetype: one card per
// symptom with a diamond kicker, serif symptom line, and labeled
// meaning/action sections; the blocked protocol closes in the
// composite's blush panel treatment.
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import docs from '../../generated/docs.json';
const mono = (s) => s.replace(/`([^`]+)`/g, '<code>$1</code>');
const headings = docs.trouble.map((t, i) => ({ depth: 2, slug: `sym-${i}`, text: t.symptom.replace(/`/g, '') }));
---
<Docs title="Troubleshooting · KeepState docs" description="Symptoms, what they mean, and what to do, synced from the operator manual." headings={headings}>
  <h1>Troubleshooting</h1>
  <p>
    <code>ks doctor</code> is the first move, always: it is the executable
    form of every hazard this project has hit, and every gate calls it
    first. The table is synced from the operator manual.
  </p>
  <div class="grid gap-[18px] mt-6">
    {docs.trouble.map((t, i) => (
      <article id={`sym-${i}`} class="bg-white border border-sand rounded-5 p-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-[9px] mb-3">
          <span class="w-[7px] h-[7px] bg-claret rotate-45 block"></span>
          <p class="font-mono text-10 tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-claret m-0">symptom</p>
        </div>
        <p class="font-serif text-22 leading-[1.25] text-ink m-0 mb-[18px]" set:html={mono(t.symptom)} />
        <p class="text-11 font-semibold tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-taupe m-0 mb-2">What it means</p>
        <p class="text-15 leading-[1.7] text-slate m-0 mb-4" set:html={mono(t.meaning)} />
        <p class="text-11 font-semibold tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-taupe m-0 mb-2">What to do</p>
        <p class="text-15 leading-[1.7] text-slate m-0" set:html={mono(t.action)} />
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
  <div class="bg-blushBg border border-shell rounded-5 p-6 mt-9">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-[9px] mb-3">
      <span class="w-[7px] h-[7px] bg-claret rotate-45 block"></span>
      <p class="font-mono text-10 tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-claret m-0">stuck past that</p>
    </div>
    <p class="text-15 leading-[1.7] text-ink m-0">
      The product's blocked protocol applies to humans too: after three
      genuinely different failed hypotheses, stop and write down the
      symptom, the hypotheses, and the evidence. Then
      <a href="/contact">send it to us</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Docs>
